  "idiom": "Everything is engraved: hatch density is the only shading; things are specimens pinned and labelled (Fig. 3, Latin names, plate numbers). Words are written by a pen or appear as caption labels with leader lines. Vermilion is the rubric colour of old manuscripts: the sung word, a wax seal."
